									

									12 Angry Men

I recently watched this movie and it stood out the expectation which I had because of its IMDB rating. Although, I would also agree with the people saying that it is not perfect, now there are a lot of movies are out there based on courtroom drama theme but this movie might have been era defining movie if there wasn't many movies at that time.

Actually the movie, according to me, wasn't about whether the accused was guilty or not, which is still not proven (to me at least), rather it was about the portrayal the different kind of characterization of jury members, personal prejudice, conscience. It can be said that the movie did a bit of exaggeration when the member of jury found those tiny details which investigation official did not just by sitting and disccussing the matter in a room. And it also highlighted the pointed where the accused was provided a defendant who actually was not interesting in the case or in trying to defend his client (is this a normally possible situation?). 

I was frustrated and sad about the fact that how some people in a position regarded very moral and responsible can behave in as indifferent as to prioritize some personal interest or prejudice over a matter where a person's life is concerned. I hope this kind of scenario is limited to fiction only.